 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Square Root Expressions Using the Product Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1033 389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050496 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4dc7f0d4-7695-5efd-99c0-299924cc9d4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186110592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1031 "The Quotient Rule for Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1033 1474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050542 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5220265d-f52d-5c53-952c-690875cf1905" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1031 "Simplifying Square Root Expressions Using the Quotient Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1033 390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050887 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6e563fb5-2e53-5b68-a90b-a963f8d0dc96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1031 "Writing Radical Expressions Using Fractional Exponents" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1033 380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050894 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6f21843d-1a34-53a0-a3e5-e5b85146fb25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9845" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = x^5 (\\cos x)^x.$ Its derivative is given by\n\n$$\ny'(x) = x^4 (\\cos x)^x \\left( 5 + g(x) \\right).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c24da7ef-0070-5aae-bade-c82ea56476ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064146 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the function \n\n$$\ny = x^5 (\\cos x)^x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the natural logarithm of both sides and use the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =\\frac{5}{x}+(x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{5}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{5}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{5}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y = x^5 (\\cos x)^x {:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}(\\frac{5}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}(\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}(5+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = x \\ln ( \\cos  x ) - x^2 \\tan x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9846" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}.$ The derivative of this function is given by\n\n$$\ny' = -\\dfrac{g(x)(x+3)^2}{(x+5)^7}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7db11c8c-344b-5d87-a8ae-3b006e5bd92b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064147 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the function \n\n$$\ny =  \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{(x+3)^{3}}{(x+5)^{6}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((x+3)^{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((x+5)^{6}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3)-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3)-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+5)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+3}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+5} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{3}{x+3}-\\frac{6}{x+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{3}{x+3}-\\frac{6}{x+5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y =  \\dfrac{(x+3)^3}{(x+5)^6}{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{(x+3)^{3}}{(x+5)^{6}}(\\frac{3}{x+3}-\\frac{6}{x+5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)^{3}}{(x+5)^{6}}(\\frac{3(x+5)-6(x+3)}{(x+3)(x+5)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)^{3}}{(x+5)^{6}}(\\frac{-3x-3}{(x+3)(x+5)}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3(x+1)(x+3)^{2}}{(x+5)^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{3(x+1)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y = \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{x^2}{x^5+ 1}}.$  The derivative of this function is given by\n\n$$\ny' =  \\dfrac{g(x)}{3\\sqrt[3]{x(x^5+1)^4}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0cec84d-96cf-5fed-ba05-a5cfc57841a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064148 #edb/ref 1074 "Our function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{5}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2/3}}{({x}^{5}+1)^{1/3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2/3}}{({x}^{5}+1)^{1/3}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2/3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({x}^{5}+1)^{1/3}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5}+1)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}+1}\\cdot (5{x}^{4}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}+1}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y =  \\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{x^2}{x^5+ 1}}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}+1}}(\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{{x}^{5}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}+1}}(\\frac{2({x}^{5}+1)-5{x}^{5}}{x({x}^{5}+1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}+1}}(\\frac{-3{x}^{5}+2}{x({x}^{5}+1)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}+1}}(\\frac{-3{x}^{5}+2}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}({x}^{5}+1)^{3}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{x}^{5}+2}{3\\sqrt[3]{x({x}^{5}+1)^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x) = \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{-3x^5+2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186506517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186506521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186506543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186506546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064309 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/